    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 7th with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as our highest-rated start (80.98), buoyed by a favorable matchup against Rhett Lowder (xERA 4.77). While he sits in the bottom third of the order, his platoon advantage and beneficial wind conditions make him a must-start, though the 36% rain risk demands close monitoring as game time approaches. **Trea Turner** (68.63) and **Junior Caminero** (69.27) anchor the core, with **Trea Turner** specifically benefiting from J.T. Ginn\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a critical boost to our scarce stolen base category. **Kyle Schwarber** (62.66) rounds out the top-tier plays, leveraging a strong xwOBA to maintain value despite a neutral platoon matchup.\n\n**Carson Benge** (60.00) makes the cut as our final starter, capitalizing on a weak matchup against Jose Quintana (xERA 5.33) that offsets his negative platoon split. **Caleb Durbin** (41.71) remains in the lineup primarily for his elite sprint speed and the high likelihood of swiping bags against Jax, even though his spot in the #9 hole drags his efficiency score down toward the marginal threshold. Our bench remains stagnant today due to a combination of team off-days and injuries; **Yordan Alvarez**, **Hyeseong Kim**, and **Kazuma Okamoto** are unavailable due to scheduling, while **Christian Yelich** remains sidelined on the IL. We are currently navigating a thin roster with **Colt Keith**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Zac Veen**, **Luke Raley**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** held in reserve for future cycles to preserve our game caps as we monitor the volatility of these lower-order matchups.",
